0,north,"Explore the level by moving in a pattern to understand the layout and identify the stairs down, and use items and actions (search, open, kick) as needed to progress.

First, move north to the next room, then continue moving in a north-south direction to create a vertical line on the map. This will help identify any corridors or rooms that may be present. Once a vertical line is established, begin moving in an east-west direction to create a horizontal line. By moving in this pattern, we can create a grid on the map and identify any obstacles or features that are present.

As we move through the level, use the search action to identify any hidden doors or passages that may be present. If a door is found, use the open action to pass through it. If a locked door or enemy is encountered, use the kick action to try and open or defeat it.

Throughout the exploration process, keep an eye on the map and make note of any changes or discoveries that are made. If a room is encountered that appears to be a dead end, use the search action to see if there is a hidden door or passage that can be used to bypass the obstacle.

